Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/elegos/Linux-Arctis-Manager
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: linux-arctis-manager
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3,
         libcap2-bin,
         hicolor-icon-theme
Suggests: python3-torch
Description: SteelSeries Arctis manager for Linux
 Replaces the SteelSeries GG software to manage SteelSeries Arctis headsets
 on Linux. Provides a user-space daemon written in Rust and a Qt6 GUI written
 in Python for controlling equalizer settings, sidetone, ANC, LED profiles,
 and more.

Package: linux-arctis-manager-lang
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         linux-arctis-manager
Description: Standalone translation files for linux-arctis-manager
 Translation files for linux-arctis-manager's non-Python UI shells (the KDE
 Plasma widget, the GNOME Shell extension) — a standalone copy outside the
 main package's Python venv, which those UI shells can read without needing
 Python at all. Pulled in automatically by whichever of those shells you
 install; not useful on its own.

Package: linux-arctis-manager-plasma-widget
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         linux-arctis-manager,
         linux-arctis-manager-lang,
         plasma-workspace
Description: KDE Plasma widget for linux-arctis-manager
 A native KDE Plasma 6 widget (plasmoid): shows headset status and a
 configurable set of quick-access controls in the Plasma panel, positioned
 and sized by Plasma itself like the volume/network applets. Talks to the
 already-running linux-arctis-manager daemon directly over D-Bus — no
 Python process involved.

Package: linux-arctis-manager-gnome-extension
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         linux-arctis-manager,
         linux-arctis-manager-lang,
         gnome-shell (>= 45~)
Description: GNOME Shell extension for linux-arctis-manager
 A GNOME Shell extension: shows headset status and a configurable set of
 quick-access controls from the top panel. Talks to the already-running
 linux-arctis-manager daemon directly over D-Bus — no Python process
 involved. Targets GNOME Shell 45+ (ES-module extensions) only.
